 ## AC5 -- killed mid-turn

+- Wall time is `now - timestamp of the previous driver_usage row (or engage
+  baseline) for this story and session`. It is recorded on every row.
 - Readers report whatever the record already contains:
   - claude transcript: the usage of assistant messages written so far,
     including a partial final message
   - codex: the last `token_count` event
   - grok: `usage.json` as last flushed
+- When the record exists but contains no usage for the turns after the
+  high-water mark (no partial turn), the recorder writes `available:false`,
+  `unavailable_reason: "<adapter>: no partial-turn usage in session record"`
+  plus `wall_seconds`, with token fields absent.
 - Test fixtures:
   - a claude transcript truncated mid-message, where the usage that is
     present is recorded
   - a grok `usage.json` identical to the previous snapshot while wall time
-    advanced
+    advanced, which gives the unavailable row plus wall time and no token
+    fields
+
+SweepDriverWindows runs across every session with an open or pending window,
+not just the current one, from four triggers: every recordDriverUsage call; a
+lease steal or stale-seat reap in acquireEngagementLease/single_story.go,
+where the dead holder's window is swept before the new baseline
+(lease.OutcomeStolen, used at single_story.go:66/345); the SessionStart hook,
+which all three adapters install; and story cost / session query. Wall time
+is bounded by the later of the record's last timestamp and the lease
+heartbeat (engagement_lease carries heartbeat_at and session_id,
+lease/store.go:51,74), not by when the kill is detected.
